The item values are rounded, the total is not.

lib/WWW/PayPal/API/Orders.pm:129 sums $unit * $qty over the raw values, while every item amount is rounded on its own by _money (:86-89). That contradicts the rule of the distribution (.claude/skills/paypal-integration/SKILL.md:175-179: "Round once ... derive the total from the parts").

Example: items => [{name => 'x', unit_amount => '0.125', quantity => 2}] gives an item amount of '0.12' (a sum of 0.24) against an item_total of '0.25'. PayPal answers 400 UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY ("item_total must match the sum of items"). In JPY, unit_amount => 10.5 with quantity => 3 gives '10' per item (a sum of 30) against an item_total of '32'.

Decide: the item_total is summed over the already rounded item amounts.

2026-10-20 09:18 Done: Orders::checkout sums the already rounded item amounts into amount.breakdown.item_total, so the breakdown matches the unit_amount values that are sent. Commit 26ba5f5. Also found: an item may carry a currency_code that differs from the order currency - the item amount is then rounded in the item currency, the sum in the order currency, which is not a meaningful sum. Behaviour left untouched (no croak, no warn), PayPal rejects a mixed-currency breakdown anyway.
